          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قصر (qaṣr) is filed by Lane under the root q-ṣ-r, \"to confine, to keep within\". It was borrowed from Aramaic qaṣrā (EtymDB), which is usually traced to Latin castra, a camp; the Latin step is not settled."
