              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تاج (tāj) was borrowed from Middle Iranian (Parthian) tāg, \"a crown\" (EtymDB), an old borrowing; Aramaic tāgā is its cousin. Arabic made a verb from it: tawwaja, to crown."
